        "original_id": "c4930f0b-abea-5df1-b4be-c6735540d97b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lantana, Silybum, milk thistle\n- Animals: Strymon bazochii\n- Taxonomy: Verbenaceae, daisy family\n- Places: Hawaii\n- Topics: biological control\n\nFacts:\n- Lantana is a genus of about 150 species of perennial flowering plants in the verbena family Verbenaceae.\n- Silybum, also known as milk thistle, is a genus of two species of thistles in the daisy family.\n- Strymon bazochii was introduced to Hawaii in 1902 to control Lantana species.\n- Strymon bazochii has proven unsuccessful at controlling Lantana species in Hawaii.",
